                     /note="Domain:cl19824:Alpha-E A predicted alpha-helical
                     domain with a conserved ER motif. An uncharacterized alpha
                     helical domain containing a highly conserved ER motif and
                     typically found as a tandem duplication. Contextual
                     analysis suggests that it functions in a distinct peptide
                     synthesis/modification system comprising of a
                     transglutaminase, a peptidase of the NTN-hydrolase
                     superfamily, an active and inactive circularly permuted
                     ATP-grasp domains and a transglutaminase fused N-terminal
                     to a circularly permuted COOH-NH2 ligase domain.
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:515-830, Eval:5.8e-64, score:214.5]"
