                     these DH domains are double hotdogs in which the active
                     site contains a histidine from the N-terminal hotdog and an
                     aspartate from the C-terminal hotdog. Studies have
                     uncovered that a substrate tunnel formed between the DH
                     domains may be essential for loading substrates and
                     unloading products. [Superfamily, Aligned:5-114,
