                     /note="Domain:cl27726:Secretin Bacterial type II and III
                     secretion system protein. Several related protein families
                     encode outer membrane pore proteins for type II secretion,
                     type III secretion, and type IV pilus formation. This
                     protein family appears to encode a secretin for pilus
                     formation, although it is quite different from PilQ.
                     Members include the PilN lipoprotein of the plasmid R64
                     thin pilus, a type IV pilus. Scoring between the trusted
                     and noise cutoffs are examples of bundle-forming pilus B
                     (bfpB). [Cell envelope, Surface structures, Protein fate,
                     Protein and peptide secretion and trafficking]
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:36-199, Eval:1.6e-14, score:68.6,
                     C-term missing]"
                     /note="MGA_1595"
