                     /note="Domain:cl05000:CHASE3 CHASE3 domain. CHASE3 is an
                     extracellular sensory domain, which is present in various
                     classes of transmembrane receptors that are parts of signal
                     transduction pathways in bacteria. Specifically, CHASE3
                     domains are found in histidine kinases, adenylate cyclases,
                     methyl-accepting chemotaxis proteins and predicted
                     diguanylate cyclases/phosphodiesterases. Environmental
