                     /note="Domain:cl27723:Orn_DAP_Arg_deC Pyridoxal-dependent
                     decarboxylase, C-terminal sheet domain. Two alternative
                     pathways can convert arginine to putrescine. One is
                     decarboxylation by this enzyme followed by removal of the
                     urea moeity by agmatinase. In the other, the ureohydrolase
                     (arginase) acts first, followed by ornithine decarboxylase.
                     This pathway leads to spermidine biosynthesis, hence the
                     gene symbol speA. A distinct biodegradative form is also
                     pyridoxal phosphate-dependent but is not similar in
                     sequence. [Central intermediary metabolism, Polyamine
                     biosynthesis] [Superfamily, Aligned:26-389, Eval:2.8e-81,
                     score:252.2]"
                     /note="MGA_1772"
