                     /note="Domain:cl01411:QSregVF_b Putative
                     quorum-sensing-regulated virulence factor. QSregVF_b is a
                     family of short Pseudomonas proteins that are potential
                     virulence factors. The structure of UniProtKB:Q9HY15 a
                     secreted protein has been solved and deposited as Structure
                     3npd, from pfam13652. It is predicted that these two
                     adjacent proteins form a single transcriptional unit based
                     on the prediction that together they interact with their
                     adjacent protein PotD, which is the putrescine-binding
                     periplasmic protein in the polyamine uptake system
                     comprising PotABCD. These two adjacent proteins are
                     predicted to be quroum-sensing-regulated virulence factors.
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:26-95, Eval:1.0e-33, score:108.7]"
                     /note="MGA_2457"
