                     /note="Domain:cl25576:FliI Flagellar biosynthesis/type III
                     secretory pathway ATPase [Cell motility, Intracellular
                     trafficking, secretion, and vesicular transport]. Members
                     of this protein family are the FliI protein of bacterial
                     flagellum systems. This protein acts to drive protein
                     export for flagellar biosynthesis. The most closely related
                     family is the YscN family of bacterial type III secretion
                     systems. This model represents one (of three) segment of
                     the FliI family tree. These have been modeled separately in
                     order to exclude the type III secretion ATPases more
                     effectively. [Cellular processes, Chemotaxis and motility]
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:15-447, Eval:0.0e+00, score:531.0]"
                     /note="MGA_2551"
