                     /locus_tag="LOCUS_26230"
                     /note="WP_007245369.1 CNNM domain-containing protein
                     (Pseudomonas syringae group) [pid:83.6%, q_cov:100.0%,
                     s_cov:100.0%, Eval:6.2e-196]"
                     /note="Domain:cl27264:CorC_HlyC Transporter associated
                     domain. Members of this protein family are exclusive to the
                     Bacteroidetes phylum (previously
                     Cytophaga-Flavobacteria-Bacteroides). GldC is a protein
                     linked to a type of rapid surface gliding motility found in
                     certain Bacteroidetes, such as Flavobacterium johnsoniae
                     and Cytophaga hutchinsonii. GldE was discovered because of
                     its adjacency to GldD in F. johnsonii. Overexpression of
                     GldE partially supresses the effects of a GldB point mutant
                     suggesting that GldB and GldE interact. Gliding motility
                     appears closely linked to chitin utilization in the model
                     species Flavobacterium johnsoniae. Not all Bacteroidetes
                     with members of this protein family appear to have all of
                     the genes associated with gliding motility and in fact some
                     do not appear to express the gliding phenotype.
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:55-407, Eval:1.0e-106, score:318.9]"
                     /note="MGA_2624"
