                     /note="Domain:cl26250:TPR_6 Tetratricopeptide repeat.
                     Members of this protein family are the product of one of
                     seven genes regularly clustered in operons to encode the
                     proteins of the tol-pal system, which is critical for
                     maintaining the integrity of the bacterial outer membrane.
                     The gene for this periplasmic protein has been designated
                     orf2 and ybgF. All members of the seed alignment were from
                     unique tol-pal gene regions from completed bacterial
                     genomes. The architecture of this protein is a signal
                     sequence, a low-complexity region usually rich in Asn and
                     Gln, a well-conserved region with tandem repeats that
                     resemble the tetratricopeptide (TPR) repeat, involved in
                     protein-protein interaction. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-269,
                     Eval:1.9e-54, score:174.2]"
                     /note="MGA_2764"
