                     /note="Domain:cl26726:OapA_N Opacity-associated protein A
                     N-terminal motif. This family includes the Haemophilus
                     influenzae opacity-associated protein. This protein is
                     required for efficient nasopharyngeal mucosal colonisation,
                     and its expression is associated with a distinctive
                     transparent colony phenotype. OapA is thought to be a
                     secreted protein, and its expression exhibits
                     high-frequency phase variation. This motif occurs at the
                     N-terminus of these proteins. It contains a conserved
                     histidine followed by a run of hydrophobic residues.
