                     /note="Domain:cl27026:AXE1 Acetyl xylan esterase (AXE1).
                     This family consists of several bacterial acetyl xylan
                     esterase proteins. Acetyl xylan esterases are enzymes that
                     hydrolyse the ester linkages of the acetyl groups in
                     position 2 and/or 3 of the xylose moieties of natural
                     acetylated xylan from hardwood. These enzymes are one of
                     the accessory enzymes which are part of the xylanolytic
                     system, together with xylanases, beta-xylosidases,
                     alpha-arabinofuranosidases and methylglucuronidases; these
                     are all required for the complete hydrolysis of xylan.
                     [Superfamily, Aligned:39-268, Eval:8.5e-08, score:51.0,
                     N-term missing]"
                     /note="MGA_4844"
