                     /note="Domain:cl28550:PilV Tfp pilus assembly protein PilV
                     [Cell motility, Extracellular structures]. Pilus systems
                     categorized as type IV pilins differ greatly from one
                     another, with some showing greater similarty to type II or
                     type III secretion systems than to each other. Members of
                     this protein family represent the PilV protein of type IV
                     pilus systems as found in Pseudomonas aeruginosa PAO1,
                     Pseudomonas syringae DC3000, Neisseria meningitidis MC58,
                     Xylella fastidiosa 9a5c, etc. [Cell envelope, Surface
                     structures, Protein fate, Protein modification and repair]
